Spec: SystemTemplateScript

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Orchestrate the offline render of `agent template system`: fire the `install_pre` hook through
    @import_template, then emit the two category groups a system package owns — `crds` first,
    `systems` second, each gated by @is_dir — through the shipped `template_<category>` emitters
    via @import_run, so documents reach stdout solely from the emitters' render passes. The file
    applies nothing, never touches the cluster and writes no status: it sequences two gates,
    merges hook contexts and invokes emitters. Twin notes, real diffs: ./../service/template.rhai
    and ./../tenant/template.rhai are byte-identical five-bucket twins (befores/vitals/others/
    scalables/posts), two diff hunks swap those bodies for `crds`+`systems` here; system is the
    only kind whose render lane emits CRDs. Unlike this directory's ./delete.rhai, the module
    carries zero import-time surface. The Rust lane /agent/src/template/system.sdd froze this
    emit order from its side first — its "render and emit" rule matches this file gate for gate.

Exposes:
  @run(@instance, @context) — the module's sole @fn and entry point; `template.rhai` is not in
    @ENTRY_POINT_PATTERNS, so `run` is exempt from `rhai/unused-function` through
    @ENTRY_POINT_FUNCTIONS (/agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.sdd); invoked as
    `template::run(instance, context)` by the embedded snippet of /agent/src/template/system.sdd,
    whose `let _ =` discards the returned value. The module is the default `template` of the
    system resolver chain — a package `scripts/template.rhai` shadows the whole orchestrator.

Accepts:
  @instance — the synthesized offline `#{ metadata: { name, namespace } }` @Dynamic built by the
    Rust snippet; never property-read here, forwarded verbatim into all three engine calls —
    `.metadata` reads happen only downstream, if a hook or emitter wants them.
  @context — the map ./context.rhai's @template lane produced. Read here: `package_dir`, the only
    key, twice as unguarded interpolated property reads in the gate paths. Every other key is
    consumed by the emitters and the resolved hooks.

Returns:
  No value channel of its own: the final statement is the `systems` gate block, so the implicit
    value is the unit `()` on every branch, and the Rust snippet discards it regardless.
  Rendered documents reach stdout inside the emitters' passes — a `---` line then one
    @yaml_encode document per object, the `crds` block ahead of the `systems` block — this file
    prints and captures nothing.

Raises:
  Zero @throw, zero @try of its own; nothing here is caught either:
  - Module/hook/emitter throw: @import_template and @import_run swallow only the absent-module
    and absent-`run` skip markers (@log_debug `No ${name} module, skipping.` / `No ${name}::run
    function, skipping.`); any raise by a hook or emitter — a broken `.hbs` render, a YAML decode
    failure — re-throws and aborts mid-stream: documents printed by the `crds` pass stay on
    stdout and the Rust lane turns the failure into the system-template exit-3 — the lane's loud
    cross-kind deviation, the service/tenant twins exit 1.
  - Interpreter errors at this level: @is_dir erroring on a gate path past its own semantics, or a
    `context` that stopped being a map — unreachable on the frozen flow, the ctx lane returns a
    map and every merge here is guarded (see the `package_dir`-erasure Handle).

Handles:
  - `install_pre` ships nowhere under ./agent/scripts — stock renders open with its debug skip,
    the @type_of guard sees the `()` and the ctx context stands. The category hooks
    (`install_crds_pre`/`_post`, `install_systems_pre`) are package/config-provided too, skipped
    inside the emitters the same way.
  - Absent category dir: the @is_dir gate is false and the whole bucket is skipped — no import,
    no hooks, no output — a system package may legitimately ship one of its two categories only.
  - Hook or emitter returning a non-map (skip `()` included): the running context survives — all
    three merge sites guard on @type_of == `map`; nothing here can bind `()` or a string to
    `context`, so ./delete.rhai's guard-free tofu assign has no counterpart here.
  - A hook-erased `package_dir`: the `()` interpolates into the gate strings, @is_dir answers
    false and the run completes silently with an empty document stream (the twins' posture).
  - Package-shadowed emitter without a `run` fn: the run shim is `run`-only — its skip marker
    prints and the bucket silently contributes no documents (Tasks).

Must:
  Execute exactly once, in this order: @import_template("install_pre", @instance, @context) with
    the map-guarded merge; then the @is_dir gates over `context.package_dir` + `/crds` and
    `/systems` with their @import_run("template_crds") / @import_run("template_systems")
    emissions in that order and no statement after the systems block (no close, no
    `install_post`). Nothing in the file reads `instance`. The order is the ./install.rhai build
    order (`crds → tofu → systems`) minus the unrenderable tofu category — not the ./delete.rhai
    reverse.
  Read each gate path off the CURRENT `context` — an `install_pre` replacement changes both probed
    dirs and both emitters' render input — and rebind only through the @type_of == `map` guard at
    all three sites, a non-map value dropped unlogged.
  Split the shims as written: `install_pre` resolves with @import_template (module `template`
    preferred, `run` fallback), the two emitters with @import_run (`run` only) — and the shipped
    emitters define nothing but `run`.
  Resolve every module name over the Rust lane's four resolver dirs, package `scripts` first: a
    package copy of `template_crds` or `template_systems` shadows the shipped emitter; names
    resolve against `scripts/system` only, never across kind directories.
  Hold zero import-time surface: no import statement, the body is the single @fn declaration — as
    in the service/tenant twins; the import-bearing orchestrator of the lane set is ./delete.rhai.
  Keep this level free of cluster calls, file reads other than the two @is_dir probes, and
    @print; fetching, rendering and emission are owned by ./template_crds.rhai (unspecified, role
    frozen by /agent/src/template/system.sdd) and ./../lib/install_from_dir.sdd respectively.

Must not:
  Fire the per-category hooks at this level: `install_crds_pre`/`install_crds_post` and
    `install_systems_pre` belong inside the emitters — duplicating them here would double-run
    package hooks.
  Grow befores/vitals/others/scalables/posts, tofu, init-from or backup lanes: the frozen lane
    probes `crds` and `systems` only; the manifest buckets belong to the service/tenant render
    twins and the tofu machinery to the live lanes.

Depends on:
  ./template_crds.rhai, ./template_systems.rhai — shipped here, both unspecified; roles as frozen
    upstream: the crds emitter is bespoke (per-file decode-and-render, a kind filter keeping
    `CustomResourceDefinition` documents, `install_crds_pre`/`_post` around it), the systems
    emitter is the shared bucketed @template pass of ./../lib/install_from_dir.rhai with
    `install_systems_pre` and no post slot. Roles quoted only; their contracts are theirs.
  vynil-core 0.7.7 engine API — the 3-arg @import_run and @import_template shims behind @Script
    @add_common (skip-vs-rethrow boundary, import_template's `run` fallback), @is_dir, @type_of.
  ./context.rhai (./context.sdd) + ./../lib/build_context.rhai — producer of the incoming map;
    key contract owned by ./../lib/build_context.sdd.
  /agent/src/template/system.sdd — the Rust lane: engine, four resolver dirs, synthesized
    instance, nine-key `args`, stdout channel and the exit-3 error lane all raises land in.

References:
  ./../service/template.sdd + ./../service/delete.sdd — calibration siblings: shared
    gate/merge/hook idiom, skip-marker quotes, and the render-lane hook-pair and shared-hook-name
    open points this file inherits.
  ./../service/template.rhai (+ byte-identical ./../tenant/template.rhai, ./../tenant/template.sdd)
    — the five-bucket, crds-void render lanes; their crds-omission open point is this lane's
    crds-first flip side.
  ./install.rhai (./install.sdd) + ./delete.rhai (./delete.sdd) — live-lane siblings of this
    directory whose category set and order this render mirrors.
  /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs — harness that never imports this module (Tasks).

Scenario: full two-category render with both directories present
  Given a package dir with `crds` and `systems` populated, no package hooks, on a live engine
  When @run executes
  Then the calls land in exactly install_pre-skip → template_crds → template_systems order
  And stdout carries the `---`+documents CRD block first, in the emitter's file-iteration and
    kind-filter order, then the `systems` documents in the shared pass's first/middle/last order
  And `context` survives every merge site and the run ends on `()`
  No mapped test: no harness imports this module.

Scenario: single-category package renders one block
  Given a package with only `systems` populated (or symmetrically only `crds`)
  When @run executes
  Then the absent category's gate skips its bucket whole — no import, no hooks — while the
    present one renders normally and the run still ends cleanly
  No mapped test.

Scenario: bare package renders nothing but skip logs
  Given a package tree with neither category dir and no hook module
  When @run executes
  Then the hook skips, both gates read false, stdout carries no documents and the run ends cleanly
  No mapped test.

Scenario: install_pre takes over the render
  Given a package `install_pre` whose `run` returns a map carrying a rewritten `package_dir`
  When the first guard accepts it
  Then both gates probe the new dirs and the emitters render the installed map
  But given the hook returning `()` or a string, the ctx context stands and the gates keep
    probing the original `package_dir`
  No mapped test.

Scenario: run-only hook executes on the offline lane
  Given a package `install_pre` defining only a cluster-touching `run`
  When the first @import_template probes it during `agent template system`
  Then the function-not-found leg re-imports and executes `run` — cluster reads and all — mid
    render (Tasks)
  No mapped test.

Scenario: mid-render emitter throw loses systems and exits 3
  Given a broken `.hbs` under `crds` and a populated `systems` dir
  When the render error crosses @import_run — not a skip marker — and re-throws
  Then `template_systems` never runs, the already-printed CRD documents stay on stdout, and the
    Rust lane exits 3 — the only template leaf not exiting 1
  No mapped test.

Scenario: a bucket shadow lacking `run` renders silently empty
  Given a package `template_crds.rhai` whose only fn is `template`, `crds` dir present
  When @import_run resolves it
  Then `No template_crds::run function, skipping.` is debug-logged and the bucket emits nothing —
    the run shim never tries `template`
  No mapped test.

Tasks:
  [ ] Map the Scenarios to /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs (or a sibling harness): nothing imports
      system/`template` and the harness resolver dirs ship `scripts/service` + `scripts/lib` only;
      add a `scripts/system` entry plus a fixture package with `crds`/`systems` dirs and pin at
      least order, single-category, bare-package, rethrow and merge-guard.
  [?] `install_pre` opens this lane while `install_post` never closes it — that hook fires only
      on the live lane (./install.rhai). The same asymmetry is open in ./../service/template.sdd;
      decide the render-lane hook-pair symmetry for all three lanes once.
  [?] Hook names shared with the live install lane: `install_pre` here and the emitters'
      `install_crds_pre`/`_post` and `install_systems_pre` are the live lane's names, and
      @import_template's `run` fallback executes a run-only cluster-touching copy mid-render.
      Decide whether the render lane gets its own hook names.
  [?] Only kind rendering CRDs: the service/tenant render lanes are crds-void (their specs' open
      point) while this lane emits `crds` first. Record the decision so the three-kind story is
      either crds-in-render everywhere or a justified system special case.
  [?] A gate-true bucket whose shadow lacks `run` loses the whole render to one debug line —
      silent output loss indistinguishable from an empty dir. Decide whether the render lane
      should hard-fail when a gated bucket fails to resolve an emitter.

Done when:
  Every Scenario carries a mapped test or a recorded decision, the gate/order/merge texts above
    still match ./template.rhai, the emitter-role delegation still resolves in
    /agent/src/template/system.sdd and ./../lib/install_from_dir.sdd, and `specdd lint` is green
    on this file.
